{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"leading-timeless-meadowlark","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Origin\nExtracted from decision register twofaced-paralytic-elk (9c72-c44a-3421-45ad), which is being dissolved into per-item tickets. Source bug: afflicted-hexed-arthropods (5b32-37c4-f99a-4315, closed) — code-review config gates enablement, not enforcement.\n\n## Decision required (verbatim from the register)\nChoose code-review invocation/enforcement semantics. Recommended compatible contract: explicit CLI/library/MCP `review-code` always runs by sending `enabled=True`; retain `verify.enable_code_review` only as the default for direct/internal verdict production; keep the Gerrit adapter explicit override because deployed receiver activation is already its enforcement control. Alternative: introduce a true `enforce_code_review` key, wire Gerrit voting to it, and coordinate repository plus deployed receiver configuration atomically so the currently-live LLM-Review gate is not silently disabled.\n\n## Status\nAwaits an operator design ruling; held at `idea` until ruled.","id":"7da9-4139-4c7f-4db2","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["decision-register","debug-sweep"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Design ruling: code-review invocation/enforcement semantics (enable vs enforce)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787438054900753001,"uuid":"8667ad61-0e21-4833-aa7c-9950d0fbd115"}